3. Technical Architecture

3.1 Tech Stack

Layer: Frontend — Technology: React + TypeScript + Vite — Version: 19.x
Layer: CSS — Technology: Tailwind CSS — Version: 4.x
Layer: State — Technology: Zustand — Version: 5.x
Layer: UI Library — Technology: ShadCN (Radix-based) — Version: latest
Layer: Backend — Technology: .NET (ASP.NET Core) — Version: 10.0
Layer: ORM — Technology: Entity Framework Core — Version: 10.0
Layer: Database — Technology: PostgreSQL — Version: 16
Layer: Payments — Technology: Stripe — Version: v52
Layer: Image Processing — Technology: SixLabors.ImageSharp — Version: 3.1
Layer: Hosting — Technology: Railway (backend + frontend + DB)
Layer: Frontend Deploy — Technology: Railway (frontend moved from Vercel)

3.2 Architecture Pattern

Clean Architecture with separation of concerns:
- webapp.Domain/        → Entities, DTOs, interfaces
- webapp.Application/   → Service interfaces
- webapp.Infrastructure/ → EF Core, services, repository
- webapp.Server/        → Controllers, middleware, startup
- webapp.SharedServices/ → Cross-cutting (auth, audit, email)
- shireenbynaeema-store/ → React SPA frontend

3.3 Infrastructure

- Containerized via Docker (multi-stage build)
- Database migrations managed via EF Core
- Image storage local to Railway with persistent volume (backups recommended)
- Frontend hosting moved to Railway (single Railway project hosts backend, frontend, and DB for simplified deployment)
- Global query filters for soft delete across all entities
- Audit logging on all CRUD operations
- Swagger/ReDoc API documentation at /swagger and /docs

